.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env

projects/*/pages/
projects/*/final/
projects/*/defects.jsonl
projects/*/*.pdf
projects/*/source/
projects/*/.flow-scratch/
projects/**/*.png
projects/**/*.jpg

# comic-corpus: third-party copyrighted pages — analysis stays in git, raw pages never do
research/comic-corpus/corpus/*/pages/

# comic-corpus catalog: raw WP API responses are re-derivable — derived records stay in git
research/comic-corpus/catalog/raw/

# comic-corpus B1: the user's raw SCRIPT text stays local; normalized records are versioned
research/comic-corpus/corpus/*/source.*
research/comic-corpus/scripts-raw/*
!research/comic-corpus/scripts-raw/README.md

# gap fix 2026-06-12: Flow zips extract as .jpeg
projects/**/*.jpeg

# publisher Wave-2: rendered crop binaries are re-derivable from the committed
# crop-specs.json + page set — the WHOLE crops/ dir (incl. its render manifest)
# stays out of git; only the specs are versioned
projects/*/posting/bundle/crops/

# EXCEPTION (2026-08-11): canonical CHARACTER REFERENCE sheets for not-so-supra-man ARE tracked.
# The blanket binary rule assumes "renders are recoverable from the Flow media ids in the ledger",
# but that assumption breaks ACROSS ACCOUNTS: these were generated on the laptop's marrtrobinson
# account and the mac mini runs growcomics, which cannot resolve those ids. Without the actual PNGs
# in git, the mini cannot attach any reference and the whole run is blocked. ~5MB, canon, one-time.
!projects/not-so-supra-man/references/characters/**/*.png
